{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops","id":1456499,"title":"What does the Syndicate use as Shock troops?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-09T23:28:13-07:00","id":1456499,"title":"What does the Syndicate use as Shock troops?","content":"I've gone through Technocracy reloaded and Syndicate revised and I'm curious what the Syndicate uses as their shock troops beyond just enforcers or regular swat teams. Do they use clones or Hit Marks like other conventions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T23:40:08-07:00","id":1456500,"title":"","content":"Mainly, it's Enforcers. For the most part, their philosophy is that if you need shock troops, you've already failed. <br /> <br /> That said, the Special Projects Division used to supply them with all manner of fringe science freaks suitable for use as shock troops if need be, such as Fomori. But that's mostly in the past, these days; and again, the Syndicate mindset is that proper preparation and techniques ranging from co-opting the enemy to \u201clet's you and him fight\u201d make Syndicate shock troops largely unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T00:53:30-07:00","id":1456503,"title":"","content":"I see the Syndicate using private military companies and hardened criminals (the kind of who do not hesitate to plant a bomb in a public place or unload with machine guns in the middle of the night) when there is a need for direct action. On the more radical side, various terrorist and paramilitary groups could also be influenced.<br /> <br /> SWAT teams I see more as an NWO asset, as controlling them requires very firm control or influence over an institution; or outright making the SWAT team and the support staff into Sympathizers. Not that it doesn't happen from time to time that the Syndicate controls such an asset, of course. An entire crew of a SWAT team could possibly be bribed or threatened into cooperation (everyone cares about their family, after all...especially after the kids are taken for a few hours drive by some strangers...) to do some tasks on their days off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-10-2021, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T01:04:26-07:00","id":1456504,"title":"","content":"Seconding the use of PMCs and criminal gangs. If the Syndicate needs raw numbers, they can be bought. Quantity has a quality all its own. You don't need to throw a small army of HIT Marks or gene-engineered soldiers at a problem, when you can just use a small number that are backed up by regular dudes with guns.<br /> <br /> Against Reality Deviants, these mundane fodder can serve the double purpose of creating a huge wall of Sleeper Witnesses to foil Traditionalists. Whether they're actual Sleepers, or Extraordinary Citizens that are primed to accept Technocratic Procedures, but not Traditionalist Effects.<br /> <br /> With enough money, any witnesses can be made to forget the Reality Deviance after the fact (possibly literally, with sufficient Mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T03:08:57-07:00","id":1456512,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy is also still one overarching organization. If they need enlightened heavy hitters, they'll just use their sway within the Union to get one of the other Conventions to do it (which is available and/or most appropriate to the problem).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T09:10:34-07:00","id":1456533,"title":"","content":"1: Use connections<br /> 2: If that fails, use money<br /> 3: If that fails, use the other conventions. <br /> <br /> I'm sure they probably do have a stash of old HIT Marks lying around for some special problem that they don't want to tell the other conventions about. I imagine the military arm of the syndicate much like the CIA. They'll do some espionage/sabotage/abductions themselves and administer information, but they'll get militias/cartels/corrupt authorities to do the heavy work. The syndicate are there for the finances. most of their fighting is done from a nice office space, with one hand on a computer and the other on a phone. The syndicate aren't going to fight a grand battle in the name of ideology like any other technocrat. Any conflict's going to have a cost-benefit analysis with a quaterly gains chart behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T16:10:28-07:00","id":1456559,"title":"","content":"So let me explain in further detail. I have a character who is a Syndicate Manager in media. Her public face is as a celebrity, pop star actress etc. I'm wondering what her &quot;security&quot; would look like if it would be plain old enforcers or if they would assign her Hit Marks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T16:26:20-07:00","id":1456561,"title":"","content":"HITMarks aren't cheap or unlimited (esp. newer models that can actually blend in well with Sleepers).<br /> <br /> So the question is more how much pull does she have? The Syndicate isn't just going to assign her powered body guards for her personal security. Because it's a bit simpler in a way: what are her Backgrounds, Merits, and Flaws? How important she is personally, or how important her friends are, or a project she's vital for, are major factors in how this would play out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T16:26:59-07:00","id":1456563,"title":"","content":"For security would look like enforcers. Syndics price themselves in being subtle. But that doesn't mean that her enforcers won't be every bit as formidable as a hit mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T18:57:23-07:00","id":1456570,"title":"","content":"CPA (Certified Public Accountant) Luchadores. Which are exactly what they sound like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T19:55:28-07:00","id":1456572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1456561#post1456561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HITMarks aren't cheap or unlimited (esp. newer models that can actually blend in well with Sleepers).<br /> <br /> So the question is more how much pull does she have? The Syndicate isn't just going to assign her powered body guards for her personal security. Because it's a bit simpler in a way: what are her Backgrounds, Merits, and Flaws? How important she is personally, or how important her friends are, or a project she's vital for, are major factors in how this would play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resources 7 fame 5, mind 4 (affinity) art 5 cha 5, she works primarily pushing ideas into the consensus through her movies, music, and social media she also does advertisements for progenitor and iteration x backed products and helps spin narratives through her social media accounts. She shows up on clean up crews to help create excuses &quot; just filming a video everyone&quot; shes the protege of the vpo of media. Her merit enchanting voice. Shes very good at what she does and her music movies and fashion lines have brought in billions in revenue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26766,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","user":"mezlabor","date":". 08-11-2021, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T03:21:44-07:00","id":1456588,"title":"","content":"She's got Resources 7, doesn't work the front-lines of the Union's battles, but in clean up? She has the best Sleeper security team money can buy, but probably that's about it. Mind 4 might mean she isn't expendable, but the rest of the things listed are something that, to the Syndicate, are replaceable enough that it's hard to justify significant assets being deployed just for her security; and you haven't listed any of the Backgrounds (Mentor/Patron, Requisitions, Backup/Retainer, etc.) that would indicate she's been working the Union to get them to value her more highly and spend more energy on her rather than expecting her to use her own wealth to cover such things. She's more than rich enough that a team of 10-12 Sleeper security experts at the absolute top of their professions including bodyguards, cyber and identity security management, and security risk assessment, would probably eat up about 1-2% of her annual income. She's that sort of rich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T04:10:21-07:00","id":1456590,"title":"","content":"I think she has enough influence within the Syndicate that they would give her a single top of the line HIT Mark bodyguard who can blend in undetectably with the rest of her Sleeper security team. I mean, it sounds like she\u2019s basically an Ariana Grande level pop star.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T04:21:47-07:00","id":1456592,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that \u201cthe best Sleeper security team money can buy\u201d is very impressive: for a Technocrat, said team almost certainly would consist of Extraordinary Citizens armed with Devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T08:00:43-07:00","id":1456600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1456588#post1456588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's got Resources 7, doesn't work the front-lines of the Union's battles, but in clean up? She has the best Sleeper security team money can buy, but probably that's about it. Mind 4 might mean she isn't expendable, but the rest of the things listed are something that, to the Syndicate, are replaceable enough that it's hard to justify significant assets being deployed just for her security; and you haven't listed any of the Backgrounds (Mentor/Patron, Requisitions, Backup/Retainer, etc.) that would indicate she's been working the Union to get them to value her more highly and spend more energy on her rather than expecting her to use her own wealth to cover such things. She's more than rich enough that a team of 10-12 Sleeper security experts at the absolute top of their professions including bodyguards, cyber and identity security management, and security risk assessment, would probably eat up about 1-2% of her annual income. She's that sort of rich.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think it was important but she does have some of those backgrounds. Full background list instead of just the highest is: resource 7 fame 5 genius 3 cult 3 (these are her most fanatical fans) status 3 mentor 2 retainer 1 backup 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26766,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","user":"mezlabor","date":". 08-11-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T15:26:16-07:00","id":1456622,"title":"","content":"Status 3 and Mentor 2 are definitely enough for, as Dataweaver pointed out, having Extraordinary Citizens with some minor Devices on top of the skills she can afford to pay for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T16:03:46-07:00","id":1456624,"title":"","content":"And don't forget that a Syndic can potentially use Management &amp; Human Resources to further bolster them, allowing them to coordinate with almost inhuman efficiency. For example, they could be so in sync with each other that is something happens to one of them, the others realize that something is off almost right away. This would make it difficult for someone to try the tactic of isolating and eliminating your team one man at a time. <br /> <br /> Basically, any Coincidental Effect that you can work that can be passed off as you directing your team in action can be cast using the management and human resources instrument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-11-2021, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T16:13:16-07:00","id":1456625,"title":"","content":"<b>Spoilers for Invincible</b><br /> <br /> &quot;You're right, you're so strong! And you, you can fly! I don't have what it takes to fight you guys. But you know what I DO have? Lots of MONEY!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>A group of dangerous mercenary supervillains are teleported into the room, punctuating the point.</i><br /> <br /> To me, this is one way to handle it. A Syndicate rep doesn't toss fireballs, but he knows a Union rep who rents out a HIT Mark for the right compensation, a rogue psychic with expensive taste in gemstones, hell even Vampires, Fomori, and sometimes Traditions Mages. Money makes the world go around, and Spheres plus Backgrounds such as Contacts and Resources do a lot.<br /> <br /> Sphere effects find useful mercenaries, Mind and Entropy tilt the negotiations in your favour, and before you know it you've got a suicide squad ready to handle dangerous elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T03:55:05-07:00","id":1457092,"title":"","content":"For the example character under discussion I would have a team of mortal bodyguards, the best money can buy. Equipped with the BEST tech money can buy. I'd have them led by an awakened enforcer from the syndicate, one trained specially as a bodyguard. At resources 7, fame 5, you really are talking about someone they can't afford to lose easily. Hit-Marks aren't good bodyguards. Sure they can fight, but thats not what bodyguards do. Bodyguards get the asset to safety as quickly and safely as possible. Hit-Marks lack the social skills to spot people exhibiting strange behaviour that could indicate a crazed superfan or (worst case scenario) a reality deviant assassin. A bodyguards top skills should be in perception, procedure and calmness under fire. Very well trained mundanes are going to be better at that than any technomantic nightmare (Hit-marks, victors, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T05:23:46-07:00","id":1457096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457092#post1457092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the example character under discussion I would have a team of mortal bodyguards, the best money can buy. Equipped with the BEST tech money can buy. I'd have them led by an awakened enforcer from the syndicate, one trained specially as a bodyguard. At resources 7, fame 5, you really are talking about someone they can't afford to lose easily. Hit-Marks aren't good bodyguards. Sure they can fight, but thats not what bodyguards do. Bodyguards get the asset to safety as quickly and safely as possible. Hit-Marks lack the social skills to spot people exhibiting strange behaviour that could indicate a crazed superfan or (worst case scenario) a reality deviant assassin. A bodyguards top skills should be in perception, procedure and calmness under fire. Very well trained mundanes are going to be better at that than any technomantic nightmare (Hit-marks, victors, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Good point. What about an Extraordinary Citizen trained as a top of the line bodyguard and also augmented with a few pieces of cyberware? As long as you don\u2019t use cyberpsychosis the cyberware should make them more effective as a bodyguard, not less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T09:19:15-07:00","id":1457105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457096#post1457096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Good point. What about an Extraordinary Citizen trained as a top of the line bodyguard and also augmented with a few pieces of cyberware? As long as you don\u2019t use cyberpsychosis the cyberware should make them more effective as a bodyguard, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it depends on the cyberware. Maybe something that provides the enhanced senses merit or additional perception. A DEI implant definitely, but I'm not sure an extraordinary citizen can handle a DEI. But a DEI with the City Eye and VDAS mobile softwares (from Technocracy Reloaded) would make for an amazing bodyguard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T09:30:41-07:00","id":1457106,"title":"","content":"I don't see why an Extraordinary Citizen couldn't handle a DEI. The only time I would put technology beyond the reach of an Extraordinary Citizen would be if the technology explicitly requires the user to make use of his own Enlightenment in order to work. In short, Inventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T10:39:15-07:00","id":1457113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457106#post1457106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why an Extraordinary Citizen couldn't handle a DEI. The only time I would put technology beyond the reach of an Extraordinary Citizen would be if the technology explicitly requires the user to make use of his own Enlightenment in order to work. In short, Inventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a problem with the DEI in M20 Technocracy Reloaded. It's listed as an &quot;Enhancement&quot; with an Enlightenment rating of N/A (page 186 M20TR). I asked about this in another thread, but never got a response and in the end my ST has me roll my own Arete rating to activate the DEI or the ES phone apps that it runs.<br /> <br /> The other post can be found here, in case you want to reference it:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455504-dei-enhancement-enlightenent-dice\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455504-dei-enhancement-enlightenent-dice\"> DEI enhancement Enlightenent dice? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455504-dei-enhancement-enlightenent-dice\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455504-dei-enhancement-enlightenent-dice </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In M20 Technocracy Reloaded, the DEI is considered an Enhancement (page 186), but shouldn&rsquo;t it have an Enlightenment rating? It can run ES-phone apps (page 180) </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T15:24:39-07:00","id":1457147,"title":"","content":"There are three circumstances I would think about and equip the team accordingly, taking into account It-X connections.<br /> <br /> 1) Driving in a car: Purchase a drone with some totally mundane features. It films the sky and displays the footage on a screen covering its underbelly, making it invisible. A laser weapon to subdue or kill attackers. A microwave gun that can disable the engine of the pursuer's vehicle. <br /> <br /> 2) At home (The drone is also used here.) <br /> <br /> - If she lives in a celebrity ego-mansion: A tower-guard at the only entrance gate. The tower is bulletproof and has a gun-turret. Belowground dog-shelters with bulletproof roofing, inhabited by guard dogs, which can be augmented. The dogs are trained to attack the legs or crotch so human security can fire guns without hitting them. <br /> <br /> - If she lives in a condo: Have two, across the street from each other. The one she lives in has a window that is a vantage point into the other. A sniper surveils the other pad, which is her listed address (or unlisted, but findable address). A decoy lives there and is ready for action.<br /> <br /> 3) At public events:<br /> With Progenitor contacts, you could have dedicated, self sacrificing vat-grown humans lacking real sentience who are the biological age of teenage fans. They are trained with simple phrases like, &quot;I won't let hurt (name of celebrity)!&quot;. They get in the way, grip attackers' arms and have strength 5. Since there are cameras everywhere, the attackers have to decide if they want to risk creating a news story in which they are filmed killing their way past such an obstruction. <br /> <br /> Besides standard bodyguards with guns and body-armor, the team could include people equipped with laptops used to control swarms of quadcopters that can navigate around crowds of people, fly up to attackers and electrocute them. <br /> <br /> When the principle participates in their own defense, a security team is more effective. This can mean knowing hot to duck and having it be reflexive or pulling out a gun - before you get to Magick. She could have a constant Mind effect on that detects murderous intent that excludes people already accounted for. Alternatively, depending on other Spheres, a telepathic message anchored to her body or clothes that reads, &quot;That's not her.&quot;. The person searching for her thinks this as if it his own thought. People she wants to interact with are made immune. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T00:34:09-07:00","id":1457190,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that Extraordinary Citizen or Technocrat bodyguards do not have to be empowered by what are often considered the default options of the Technocracy - cybernetics or superior training. There is also the option of the Progenitors being involved. Considering that Progenitors can use Treatments that modify the body and the mind, pretty much any sensible power or capability could be provided for. A Progenitor agent - Enlightened or not - could be capable of going into an Entropy 1 trance/sense that could detect hostile intent. A Life 1 or Mind 1-2 Effect could sense stress and urgency of possible attackers. They could have a broad Time 1 enhancement to know the precise time and have perfect reflexes. A specialized Time 2 divination/danger sense. Or a Time 3 haste Effect.<br /> <br /> The great benefit of having a Progenitor bodyguard is their great expertise in healing, of course. And as another benefit - the creation and providing access to psychoactive substances, just to have a bit of fun and variety on the side <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Considering the influence and position of this particular Syndicate woman, a bodyguard sent by the Progenitors could definitely do more than just protecting her. She or he could be schooled and advised in regard to manipulating the Masses, organization, influencing the mass media, and overall details of the Syndicate Paradigm (nothing that is considered a secret, of course). This way the groundwork is laid for further cooperation between the different Conventions in the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T08:54:05-07:00","id":1457271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1456561#post1456561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HITMarks aren't cheap or unlimited (esp. newer models that can actually blend in well with Sleepers).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not a simple point. (and, well, even if the mark V's can't hold a conversation, they can pass as a stoic guard) <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">First, Hypertech is bullshit and thus the economics of making these things isn't limited by money. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Technomagic is, from a certain perspective, all about circumventing the effort needed to create normal tech. You're cutting corners like crazy. The reason the Technocracy doesn't spurn Terminators out like they're iPhones is probably because of Quintessence limitations rather than money. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> There's obsolescence to consider. HIT marks I through III are questionable historical footnotes that no longer fit the technocratic paradigm, and IV probably wasn't worth using. V is where they really begin. The Not-T-800 and it's many minor variants. Only thing is, according to M20, the technocrats now have... are they on IX or X? Bearing in mind none of these are straight upgrades. The liquid metal one was too vulgar, and the newest one doesn't use much metal IIRC. You wouldn't recycle a V to make a later model, and you likely have to come up with an all-new factory for each itteration. There's going to be a lot of Obsolete Vs lying around, because unless you're extracting primium, the smartest thing to do with these old HIT marks are to send them into missions till they bust, or sell them in an attempt to recoup their loss/fund the next one: You might even be able to profit, given how even the oldest V's exceed the limits of today's tech. <br /> <br /> Lastly, and yeah this probably goes against the mindset of MAGES because they've got egos to the moon and would probably push for Gagetbahns over conventional transport every day of the weak, but the HITMARK V is a 35ish year old technology, and sure the Technocrats evidently have some &quot;Nanomachines, Son&quot; updates, but for a lot of things that work well, the next step is to make them cheaper and easier to produce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T17:05:29-07:00","id":1457357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457271#post1457271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's obsolescence to consider. HIT marks I through III are questionable historical footnotes that no longer fit the technocratic paradigm, and IV probably wasn't worth using. V is where they really begin. The Not-T-800 and it's many minor variants. Only thing is, according to M20, the technocrats now have... are they on IX or X? Bearing in mind none of these are straight upgrades. The liquid metal one was too vulgar, and the newest one doesn't use much metal IIRC. You wouldn't recycle a V to make a later model, and you likely have to come up with an all-new factory for each itteration. There's going to be a lot of Obsolete Vs lying around, because unless you're extracting primium, the smartest thing to do with these old HIT marks are to send them into missions till they bust, or sell them in an attempt to recoup their loss/fund the next one: You might even be able to profit, given how even the oldest V's exceed the limits of today's tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, or posting them as guards inside some high-value (or not-so-high-value) Construct. If they don't need to be blending in, it doesn't matter if they aren't good at it. Nor does it matter if their tech is old enough that most Traditionalists know their tricks. If Reality Deviants have breached far enough into a secure facility to face the Mark Vs, things have already spiraled out of control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, and yeah this probably goes against the mindset of MAGES because they've got egos to the moon and would probably push for Gagetbahns over conventional transport every day of the weak, but the HITMARK V is a 35ish year old technology, and sure the Technocrats evidently have some &quot;Nanomachines, Son&quot; updates, but for a lot of things that work well, the next step is to make them cheaper and easier to produce. </div> </div> </div>One could probably strip the Primium out of a Mark V, or build one without it in the first place, and use them as just a humanoid robot. The Primium is the main resource bottleneck for HITMarks. The easiest way to make one cheaper is to just to not have the Primium.<br /> <br /> The downsides, obviously, is that they're vulnerable to Reality Deviants. The upside is that you have all the other advantages of a Mark V, including being old tech that's easy to maintain. (I imagine there's quite a few Technocrats - Enlightened or otherwise - who are very familiar with how the Mark V works, and how to keep it going.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T19:30:38-07:00","id":1457365,"title":"","content":"Cause someone asked what her other spheres are life 3 entropy and time 2. Right now shes given the title PR Manager and shes a t3 middle manager with media. She has her own amalgam consisting of her &quot;manager&quot; who's from finance, her head of security an enforcer and her publicist whos also from media and is the information specialist. <br /> <br /> someone asked where she lived. She has a mansion that is indeed a shrine to her an enormous ego. Loaded with her awards trophies, platinum records, her magazine covers and spreads and movie posters. <br /> <br /> she has good relations with itx as a spokeswoman for many of their products and with the progenitors because shes run benefit concerts and celebrity fund raisers to raise money for projects disbursements denied that she still believed in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T04:53:32-07:00","id":1457386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457092#post1457092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hit-Marks lack the social skills to spot people exhibiting strange behaviour that could indicate a crazed superfan or (worst case scenario) a reality deviant assassin. A bodyguards top skills should be in perception, procedure and calmness under fire. Very well trained mundanes are going to be better at that than any technomantic nightmare (Hit-marks, victors, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I reckon with today's tech, especially with Mage schenanigans added on top, it'd be very easy for a robot to identify threats. They're likely better at it than humans. There's also the advantage Hit-Marks have in being made of very durable materials; they make excellent body shields, and feel no pain or fear. There's also the advantage of, y'know, being more &quot;switched on&quot;: Humans get tired, they get distracted, they get lazy. Droids don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T17:48:28-07:00","id":1457665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1456559#post1456559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me explain in further detail. I have a character who is a Syndicate Manager in media. Her public face is as a celebrity, pop star actress etc. I'm wondering what her &quot;security&quot; would look like if it would be plain old enforcers or if they would assign her Hit Marks</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Enforcers tend to be the equivalent of the main characters from <i>Man on Fire</i> or <i>Taken</i>, if not going into full blown <i>John Wick</i> territory. (The Ethan Hawke film <i>24 Hours to Live</i> is also a really good source of inspiration.)<br /> <br /> For my own games, I've long used various groups of specialists, including Headhunters (troubleshooters, trackers, extraction specialists - read &quot;kidnapping&quot; - and assassins), Spectres (undercover, espionage and infiltration), and White Knights (elite combat units used for security and raids). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T18:09:23-07:00","id":1457667,"title":"","content":"Yes. Remember that the Art of Desire isn't <i>just</i> about economics; it also includes a healthy dose of \u201cI can do that because I'm just that good\u201d: in effect, ruthlessly taking advantage of the Magick Enhancing Abilities (and vice versa) rules to take seemingly ordinary expertise and kick it up a notch. <br /> <br /> How do you think a Terminator would fare against John Wick? That's what could happen if a HIT Mark takes on an Enforcer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T07:28:53-07:00","id":1457788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457665#post1457665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Enforcers tend to be the equivalent of the main characters from <i>Man on Fire</i> or <i>Taken</i>, if not going into full blown <i>John Wick</i> territory. (The Ethan Hawke film <i>24 Hours to Live</i> is also a really good source of inspiration.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they really so good? I would've thought an Enforcer is just the psycho you've got with the willingness to &quot;get shit done&quot;. I don't expect a Dan in Karate. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow. I just remembered the Syndicate has ties to Pentex, and thus they could probably draw in some of the more stable Formori. Formori are cheap, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T07:45:18-07:00","id":1457790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457667#post1457667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think a Terminator would fare against John Wick? That's what could happen if a HIT Mark takes on an Enforcer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... this really depends on preperation. JW almost entirely used small calibre weapons. The Terminator is basically immune to those. If he had the foresight to use the slug-throwing shotgun that defeated those guys with magic armour in the 3rd film, he might win, but what's the chance of him having that foresight? If you're an expert, you shoot a guy, he goes down, you're not expecting him to retaliate with calm precision after you've shot him a few times. That's what a Terminator would do. Now granted, Hit Marks are a bit of a step down from the Terminator, but most enforcers, if they really are JW skilled, aren't going to have the bullet proofed suit, they aren't going to have a butler-gun merchant, and... yeah that's all i've got to say on the topic. On the otherhand, give your JW a Magick gun and the HIT Mark will almost be any-other goon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T14:33:41-07:00","id":1457827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457788#post1457788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they really so good? I would've thought an Enforcer is just the psycho you've got with the willingness to &quot;get shit done&quot;. I don't expect a Dan in Karate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate's whole schtick is &quot;the best that money can buy&quot;, and that includes both staff and training. Even in the days of Sorcerers Crusade and the High Guild, especially with the Resplendent Axe and Rose Guild, this included instruction in the martial arts. Enforcers' skill in such areas should really be roughly on par with that of the Euthanatos (probably not quite with the Akashic Brotherhood, as that is specifically the Brotherhood's niche/forte). <br /> The Swashbucklers Handbook went into more detail about the various factions of the High Guild, including pointing out that the members of the Resplendent Axe Guild (the armed guards/hired mercenaries) are expected to be as much courtiers as they are guards and enforcers. Likewise, modern Enforcers should be able to blend in with the sort of elite society their Principals are a part of. Thugs are a dime a dozen. Quality means knowing how to behave. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T00:32:44-07:00","id":1457874,"title":"","content":"Is the whole Shtick &quot;the best money can buy&quot;? I thought it was &quot;we make money&quot;. To make money, sometimes you need to save. <br /> <br /> I think it's generally going to be more cost effective to recruit several people with 6 dice of skills than it is to recruit someone who averages at around 8, nevermind low level spheres, and honestly if you can get good equipment it might be best to get a small army with average skills of 4. As good as JW is, he gets by a lot on the incompetence/foolhardyness of his enemies rather than his own skills, and for an &quot;escort mission&quot; a lot of his skills would be wasted and several professionals are going to have more of a deterrence factor than one supremely skilled mortal/low level mage<br /> <br /> Hmm. I wonder what artificial humans cost? Maybe the syndicate can order a batch of Jango-Fett clones. (who, in theory, should be JW good, but are generally mostly depicted like normal soldiers who don't mind massive casualties and stupid tactics) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T20:28:04-07:00","id":1457949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457790#post1457790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh... this really depends on preperation. JW almost entirely used small calibre weapons. The Terminator is basically immune to those. If he had the foresight to use the slug-throwing shotgun that defeated those guys with magic armour in the 3rd film, he might win, but what's the chance of him having that foresight? If you're an expert, you shoot a guy, he goes down, you're not expecting him to retaliate with calm precision after you've shot him a few times. That's what a Terminator would do. Now granted, Hit Marks are a bit of a step down from the Terminator, but most enforcers, if they really are JW skilled, aren't going to have the bullet proofed suit, they aren't going to have a butler-gun merchant, and... yeah that's all i've got to say on the topic. On the otherhand, give your JW a Magick gun and the HIT Mark will almost be any-other goon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just a matter of preparation. The original Terminator got taken out by a waitress. And she had little to no preparation. Am Enforcer vs. a HIT Mark wouldn't be the Enforcer shooting the HIT Mark with pistols until our of bullets and then standing there looking stupid until the HIT Mark walks up and comes him; he would adjust his tactics accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T20:32:56-07:00","id":1457950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457874#post1457874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the whole Shtick &amp;quot;the best money can buy&amp;quot;? I thought it was &amp;quot;we make money&amp;quot;. To make money, sometimes you need to save.</div> </div> </div> </div> And sometimes you need to know when \u201csaving money\u201d will cost you. When you're protecting a major asset, you don't want to cut corners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T05:58:47-07:00","id":1457963,"title":"","content":"She's a Manager, works in media together with the amalgam, is an <u><b>extremely public</b></u> figure, with <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Resources, Fame, </span>Cult, Status, Mentor, Retainer and Backup, and her main shtick is being a huge celebrity.<br /> <br /> A HIT Mark would be a liability. The problem isn't if the robot can pass for human, but your general level of exposition. Since you're a celebrity you're not the only one under exposure. Your security team's primary activity isn't even protecting you from danger. They must deal with all types of weirdos and fans, and they will be under continuous public scrutiny too, even if from a lesser degree. They're harassed, questioned, sometimes even interviewed themselves, they're not just security, they're YOUR security.<br /> <br /> Your work isn't to stay in a war zone, either, under attack your security team's function consists on getting you out quickly and safely, not engaging. Assessment and repositioning are more valuable skills than facing heavy artillery, in a pinch the whole team should be out of Dodge as fast as possible and call in reinforcements. The places you go are also a thing, your security team must be able to work with the staff of other places and events, they have to be accepted, make your work easier rather than harder by, lets say, punching your mom in public.<br /> <br /> Don't try to overkill. A staff member that leaves a body is better for you than one that can survive a machine gun assault in the face in front of the cameras, the best is if they can get injured and be visited by your fans in the hospital, for even better media coverage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T06:20:48-07:00","id":1457967,"title":"","content":"Right. The impression I'm getting is that you are looking for some sort of exotic or weird thing to you as your security. That's exactly the opposite of what the Syndicate would go for: they <i>like</i> it when people mistake them for Sleepers; the Awakened tend to underestimate them, and the Sleepers are more likely to engage with them. <br /> <br /> And when push comes too shove, Enforcers shouldn't be underestimated. While they don't have the raw firepower and armor of a HIT Mark (and they generally don't need it, for the reasons <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> just outlined), they're still Enlightened agents, or at least Extraordinary Citizens; and while they wouldn't fare well in a white room smackdown, that's generally not the environment that they operate in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T06:29:28-07:00","id":1457970,"title":"","content":"If they don't have a Martinez suit wielding a balefire thrower, what good is security?<br /> <br /> Alright, I've gotten a little caried away with the HIT MARKS (who wouldn't?). In my Defence, I'm sure they could cook up a version that looks like a human when you shoot holes through it.<br /> <br /> The Issue is that she's not got to just deal with superfans, but also ideological enemies, IE whatever the Traditions can throw at her. Obtaining Resources 7 by being a personality means you've got an absolute fuckton of clout, and it'd be a great idea to get rid of you, or at least throw you into some scandal.<br /> <br /> Things I'd throw my money/quintessence at if I were managing this character's protection. As said, you obviously want something &quot;exotic&quot; so I'll try my best to be exotic and... economical. <br /> <br /> 1- A body double. I'm sure the Technocracy can make these both convincing and easily disprovable as you if the enemy ever got their hands on it.<br /> 2- A large and shadowy investigative team that monitors everything and makes sure nobody can plant anything on our darling star. These fellows will likely have enhancements. They will be tasked with securing locations ahead of time, making sure no threats pop up, and will be completely deniable as to having any relation with our star.<br /> 3- an overt, lightly armed team of 6-die security, with a couple of spare AR-15's for when there's a risk of terrorism.<br /> 4- A good guy that can get the police on board with anything they do.<br /> 5-A Very defensible home<br /> 6-A drone team/Advanced surveillance tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T07:23:12-07:00","id":1457975,"title":"","content":"Earlier, someone made a brief mention of SPD \u2014 or rather, they talked about how the Syndicate has ties to Pentex, which unfortunately tends to be treated as synonymous with SPD. I have my own take on what SPD is; and if you can talk your Storyteller into accepting this notion, it opens up some additional opportunities. <br /> <br /> In my view, SPD is less about Pentex and its service to the Wyrm, and is more about fringe science: the Fringe TV Series would be one example of an SPD-centered chronicle. Your diva isn't SPD; but she could have her security team requisition some great from them; and that gear could include countermeasures for Magick. If you're familiar with <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b>, Task Force Valkyrie's Advanced Tech includes a lot of stuff that would work well as products of this not blatantly corrupt take on SPD. <br /> <br /> In short, if you're concerned with your diva being attacked by supernatural forces, you can equip her security detail with gear that's designed to deal specifically with supernatural threats. The Syndicate would still likely insist that whatever you come up with be as Coincidental as possible; e.g., special rounds for their guns that harm spirits and ghosts of you're concerned with the Traditionalists using Spirit Magick against her, and/or visors based on the principles of Kirlean photography that let the agent see so-called \u201cmystical energies\u201d so that he's aware of incoming threats of that nature. <br /> <br /> My earlier mention of how the Management &amp; HR instrument can be applied factors in here, too: if the security chief is Enlightened and has some knowledge of Dimensional Science, he could use Management &amp; HR to make the security team's perimeter patrols double as a ward against intrusion by spiritual entities. <br /> <br /> The point is that you don't need to have the security team be ignorant of our defenseless against supernatural vectors of attack; they're just not going to be blatant about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T07:42:36-07:00","id":1457976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't have a Martinez suit wielding a balefire thrower, what good is security?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone have to take the dangerous but boring job of walking around naked. I mean, without proper basic artillery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- A body double. I'm sure the Technocracy can make these both convincing and easily disprovable as you if the enemy ever got their hands on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure things. Even RL celebs get those sometimes, she probably have at leas a couple of hypertech body doubles. One of them can even BE a HIT Mark in disguise, for tactical deployment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- A large and shadowy investigative team that monitors everything and makes sure nobody can plant anything on our darling star. These fellows will likely have enhancements. They will be tasked with securing locations ahead of time, making sure no threats pop up, and will be completely deniable as to having any relation with our star.</div> </div> </div> </div>The direct security team isn't even probably more than a fifth of her entire staff. As Syndicate Manager with high-profile public activity she will have the best of the best, equipped with state-of-the-art Technocratic equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- an overt, lightly armed team of 6-die security, with a couple of spare AR-15's for when there's a risk of terrorism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't shy from going for 8-dice team, or at least a couple 8-dice members sourced from ex-military and intelligence agencies. She does have Resources 7, she isn't just rich, she is VIP enough for her assassination to have repercussions on the global economy and send her base city into a financial crisis. She shouldn't have a too overt team, but the best money can buy is quite for real here, even without Technocratic links.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4- A good guy that can get the police on board with anything they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only the police, but city administration in general. This is the channel to go when you need to close entire avenues for shooting a film, as an example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5-A Very defensible home</div> </div> </div> </div>At home HIT Marks are fair play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457970#post1457970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6-A drone team/Advanced surveillance tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two, actually, one overt and one secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T09:14:04-07:00","id":1457979,"title":"","content":"I think, in general, if you're overtly asking for a full team of 8 die security, you're pretty sus, doesn't matter how much money you have, a non-governmental figure shouldn't have many bodyguards from the SAS or what have you. 6 die security are competent and plentiful. Plenty of voluntary service members will have those specs. 8 die security are limited, and you have to ask yourself why do you need so many one-man armies for a protection detail when you could hire them for something that demands their skillset. The issue is less money and more that there aren't that many of them and I'm sure that unless the technocracy has some kind of Kamino base, the Syndicate would have better use for such elites. If you had one former SAS member and the rest where above average infantry (Paratroopers, Rangers, Commandos, NCOs) it'd be quite understandable and price-performance you'd do a lot better. You might even get some people that occasionally veer into that 8 dot range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T10:50:24-07:00","id":1457987,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, I work at a big bank IRL. We have a concept in the industry where starting at a certain level of assets a client gets very special treatment. It isn't simply special service, it is every rule for the business being different to account for for two factors: how much increased risk the client is at because of their position and how much the economy as a whole can suffer if something is out of place.<br /> <br /> Of course this is partly the bank giving nice VIP treatment to the \u00fcber rich, but this is also because if the owner of a factory chain have a silly problem and can't access her bank account for a couple days this can effectively disrupt jobs, payments, negotiations and food supplies in a large scale. This person is so important that we actually cannot give her normal treatment not even if she asks. She isn't a person, she's a community's asset.<br /> <br /> We are not the only industry to do this, either, and in several instances this treatment is required by law. That's the thing I said about her being too VIP. Her security IS top priority. If she is that influential and rich she is at least like Oprah. She can be the target of a terrorist attack, she can be targeted by foreign countries, she attracts wacko fans that aren't just kids anymore. And her work moves an industry. As OP said, she already brought BILLIONS in revenue to the Syndicate, and that through absolutely clean, proper and public means, so she pretty much moves a sector of the media industry.<br /> <br /> Also, former members of special services working in the private sector aren't only a thing, they're a relatively common thing. Not hugely common, but there is a number of high-end private security services that operate this way, employing precisely that kind of person. So her personal attachment having 2 to 6 top-notch ex-military, FBI or CIA isn't at all that unthinkable (and hey, despite their skill level, they're still normal people that need normal jobs after leaving service).<br /> <br /> This is all in the realm of possibility, and all considering only her mundane side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T12:17:29-07:00","id":1457990,"title":"","content":"Yes, ex Special forces apparently make up half the private mercenaries. They're the guys crazy enough to dedicating their life to war for money... I suppose it makes sense to give her ALL the elites<br /> <br /> 7 dots of resources is the beyond the point of what the fuck do can you do to spend this money, buy a second or third rate country as your private property? Single and simultaniously handily finance movies for every hero DC has? <br /> <br /> She should be investing in DEUS EX(the original) style security bots for her own private security. Considerably less vulgar than HIT MARKS. (imagine a pop star supporting killbot companies. It'd be funny) <br /> (I mean, if she just patronizes the companies that make these killbots, it wouldn't be that weird) <br /> <br /> 6 resources exists just to snub people with 5 resources. 7 dots is silly money (Though, if each dot of resources is Dots x Last level number of dots, so 3 dots of resources makes 3 times the amount 2 dots makes, and we assume 1 dot is a developed nation's min wage, you still don't have Bezos money with 10 dots of resources) <br /> <br /> <br /> A personality worth 7 dots of resource is going to be the frontman of the technocratic union, and one of the greatest entertainers in the world. There might be Technocrats richer, but they aren't going to be public figures. You are going to be one of the biggest main characters in the Ascension war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T12:00:53-07:00","id":1458393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1457990#post1457990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. There might be Technocrats richer, but they aren't going to be public figures. You are going to be one of the biggest main characters in the Ascension war.</div> </div> </div> </div>That combined with her Fame 5 is one of the reasons I figured she would be a very important player with the Syndicate. <br /> <br /> She does have some high profile enemies. The worst being a 3 pt enemy flaw a Toreador superfan, shes become the object of his art obession. While he doesnt want to kill her, he does want to turn her into his ghoul. Which might be just as bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T16:39:50-07:00","id":1458582,"title":"","content":"She isn't just an important player with the Syndicate, the good part is that she's an important player on Sleeper society. You should take care with too strange guards around her because she's high profile, but no one will find it unreasonable for her to have over-the-top security publicly. There are CIA agents dreaming with working for her after retirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T22:34:41-07:00","id":1458618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458582#post1458582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She isn't just an important player with the Syndicate, the good part is that she's an important player on Sleeper society. You should take care with too strange guards around her because she's high profile, but no one will find it unreasonable for her to have over-the-top security publicly. There are CIA agents dreaming with working for her after retirement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking the enforcer who works as her head of security will lead a team of unenlightened t0 PMCs . Those will be mundane but top of their game, ex intelligence ex spec ops etc. They'll probably have drones, armored cars etc. Someone mention body doubles and cloned &quot;fans&quot; that can be planted and rush attackers while her security rushes her out of hostile situations. <br /> <br /> The supernatural stuff I'm not real sure on. She's going to need protection from that as well. Especially the vampires enemies she has. Shes clashed with the Toreador and the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T03:57:48-07:00","id":1458641,"title":"","content":"<b>Ascension's Landscape</b> (Storyteller's Vault) talks about this issue in a more general way: celebrities and the wealthy have tremendous mundane power, and most of them don't have the means to defend themselves against supernatural influence; so why isn't every last one of them in the thrall of some supernatural forces or another? The book goes through several possible answers for that, all of which boil down to some variation of \u201cthere is some one or some thing that's looking out for the rich and famous, and anyone who decides to target them will end up running into it.\u201d<br /> <br /> One fairly simple suggestion that out makes is that there might be an ongoing worldwide Effect that automatically provides countermagic against mental influence based on how much Resources you have: in practical terms, it lets you use your Resources Background as countermagic dice on any attempt to apply mental influence to you. I mention it to illustrate the sorts of possibilities the book suggests; I would definitely recommend picking it up and considering its advice where this diva is concerned. <br /> <br /> And again, the Technocracy has been in a war against supernatural powers since its founding; and at least as of Technocracy Reloaded, the notion that they don't <i>believe</i> in the supernatural has been buried. It stands to reason, then, that they would have developed countermeasures against supernatural interference. See my earlier post for some further thoughts on this direction. <br /> <br /> But another possibility would be to say that there <i>are</i> some Technocrats who flat-out don't believe in magic, and who are in Denial; and that some of these end up weaponizing their Denial along the lines of the way that Marauders weaponize Madness: see Negation Men in <b>Book of Secrets</b>. Including <i>one</i> Negation Man in her entourage would throw a monkey wrench into the plans of any magickal threats aimed at her. (Though you might want to tweak the Negation Man concept slightly if you do this; as written, they're more like the Autumn People from Changeling, wed to extreme mundanity and equally a threat to technomancers and mystics alike.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T03:58:26-07:00","id":1458643,"title":"","content":"You don't need HIT Marks for those, you need preparation. And Technocratic equipment, just subtler than killing robots. Bullets that seek the heart carrying a piece of wood, others that explode in silver shrapnel inside the target (bullets that kinda explode inside the target are already a thing IRL), and most importantly, remember the basics of their work: you don't have to fight back, you have to back away. The Union have other teams to hunt down and exterminate greater threats.<br /> <br /> That going to the extremes. Protections against mental tampering and some similar resources are enough to deal with most supernaturals whose goals and methods are still civilized. Your main Toreador threat is an uncouth fan? The role of her security is to keep the vampire from harming and Ghouling, not from being annoying.<br /> <br /> Instead of focusing in security, or better, on her bodyguards, think about her staff as a whole. Have someone analyzing her food and drinks before she consumes, if it can't be done from a distance with Enlightened methods, then pose a poisoning attempt to justify this level of paranoia as an empathetic quirk. Hack cameras in the area to detect supernatural presences before they strike. Remember that you don't have to take BS from RDs if they're too troublesome, you can call a squad to hunt down the problem if need be. This Toreador mere existence is only acceptable to the Union as far as it stays out of the way and out of problem.<br /> <br /> Some problems are still her in the end, as they are for any celebrity. Problematic fans happen. Her security system is there for the protection of her integrity, but she is her own main public relations guy. Talk with the vampire, try to reason, and use Magick if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T11:59:28-07:00","id":1458704,"title":"","content":"We're also talking about a character with Mind 4. She has the magical oomph to deal with Presence and Dominate. It's just the normal equation with mages vs. other supernaturals: time to prepare. Without time, vampire Disciplines are much more effective. With time, she can quite easily ensure her safety from crafty blood-suckers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T13:27:08-07:00","id":1458718,"title":"","content":"If it matters these are the relantionships she has with other conventions from best to worst<br /> <br /> Syndicate. She makes money, lots of money, she wields social influence, lots of social influence, she gets the job done so they tend to overlook some of her more lax attitudes.<br /> <br /> Progenitors. Life is one of her strong spheres and she partners with the progenitors on her line of health and beauty products, She also partners with progenitor doctors when she visits children's hospitals to help spur along the kids healing. She always makes sure these visits help the kids recovery in ways that dont discredit the progenitors or are too obviously her doing. If disbursements denies funding to a progenitor project she believes in she will arrange her own benefit concerts or celebrity charity fundraisers to raise money for these projects outside the syndicate. More then a few progenitor researchers owe her a favor or two as a result.<br /> <br /> Iteration X. Pretty straight forward one of her roles is to be a spokeswoman for products. So many an Iteration X product will have commercials starring her, or wind up with product placements in her movies and videos or shout outs on her social media. Being extremly charismatic shes often tapped by them to be a spokesperson at conventions and has been a VC for a number of ItX tech startups.<br /> <br /> Void Engineers. She doesnt understand them, doesnt understand what they do. She respects them but they work on opposite sides of reality and rarely ever interact<br /> <br /> The New World order. Often rivals. She works doing work very similar to what they do shaping consensus, but shes a lot less rigid and orthodox. They all wear the same black suits and mirrored shades, she wears flamboyant designers labels. Not all of them like that she questions if the Union always goes about things in the best and most fair way. The Syndicate let her get away with some of her more controversial views because she gets results but it might not fly if she were in the NWO. Some of them think she may be a little too wrapped up in being a celebrity and may need a reminder that being a member of the Union isnt always starring in movies, album release parties, celebrity galas, and awards shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26766,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","user":"mezlabor","date":". 09-04-2021, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T16:46:03-07:00","id":1458744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458618#post1458618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking the enforcer who works as her head of security will lead a team of unenlightened t0 PMCs . Those will be mundane but top of their game, ex intelligence ex spec ops etc. They'll probably have drones, armored cars etc. Someone mention body doubles and cloned &quot;fans&quot; that can be planted and rush attackers while her security rushes her out of hostile situations.<br /> <br /> The supernatural stuff I'm not real sure on. She's going to need protection from that as well. Especially the vampires enemies she has. Shes clashed with the Toreador and the Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>An enlightened Enforcer is not going to just sit back and hope known, identifiable threats don't come knocking. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458643#post1458643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that you don't have to take BS from RDs if they're too troublesome, you can call a squad to hunt down the problem if need be. This Toreador mere existence is only acceptable to the Union as far as it stays out of the way and out of problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character and her Enforcer have a lot of advantages in this situation. If I read your posts above correctly, the Toreador is allied to one or more Ventrue. You want to shatter that alliance to isolate the obsessed Toreador. If your character has a social science background, she would be familiar with Obsessive Love Disorder, which the Toreador suffers from, magnified by Vampirism. In his haven, the Toreador watches her on a screen - technology. Ask It-X to spare someone with Matter and Forces to accompany her to his haven during the daytime. She can use Mind on ghouls and retainers to put them in a daze. The It X Mage unlocks the door, finds the Toreador's media shrine and then uses Matter and Forces to alter flat-screens/monitors so that they have hidden cameras filming him, sending the data to the security team. Bug his car and phone(s) in the same way. <br /> <br /> Do the same to the Ventrue. Discover how he controls his money and assets. Is it in the name of a ghoul or does he use a fake identity to maintain claim over his assets? Prepare to unravel his fake claim over his fortune.<br /> <br /> It's a multi-jurisdiction crime happening. It's likely the Ventrue who control local police there. Get eyes and electronics inside the local police station to document any cover up they are made to do on behalf of the Toreador. Have the police where she is share intelligence with local police early in the morning, followed immediately by a letter from her legal team, insisting that they take action to fullfill their duty of protection. This is going to force the Ventrue to spend willpower to attempt to interfere, when his police lackey calls his haven. Unable to go anywhere, he has to communicate by phone or have his in-house ghouls pass on messages. Record everything. <br /> <br /> She's in Media. Create a newscast exposing it all, while filtering out evidence of their Vampirism. Focus on the Inhumanity of the perpetrators so that other Vampires question if these two are fit to be Undead. While he is publicly implicated in a police cover-up, send evidence of the fuckery the Ventrue uses to control his assets to independent auditors acting in public interest or Syndicate IRS people. Strip the Ventrue of his precious fortune.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458643#post1458643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talk with the vampire, try to reason, and use Magick if needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventue, maybe, not the Toreador. In cases of stalking, the stalker's belief that he is destined to be with the victim is reinforced by any voluntary communication initiated by the victim, no mater what the victim says. Using surveillance to prove a pattern of behavior with a scientific diagnosis, Obsessive Love Disorder, she could put together a well presented film for the Ventrue alone to see. Avoid direct contact with the Ventrue, in case he would try to capture your character and hand her over to the Toreador. A currier sent during the day works. He can view it at dusk when his butler or whoever brings it to him. It's up to the Ventrue if he wants to interrupt the Toreador's descent into madness. He might Dominate the Toreador and say, &quot;Listen, you need to find a new muse...&quot; -reasons, etc. <br /> <br /> Another angle could be to gather evidence of anything the Ventrue has done to mess with your character and use it to claim she is in danger from the Ventue. An anonymous person sends this to the Toreador. Use Mind to convince him. All she has to do is hide for a while. The Toreador will immediately assume the role of protector. Unable to locate her, he will move against the Ventrue, confront him with accusations or appeal to a Prince, Archon, etc., who will likely figure out that he's insane, responding accordingly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T17:35:33-07:00","id":1458749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458744#post1458744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ventue, maybe, not the Toreador. In cases of stalking, the stalker's belief that he is destined to be with the victim is reinforced by any voluntary communication initiated by the victim, no mater what the victim says.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but it doesn't matter. She have Mind 4. Cut the middle man and cure the Toreador.<br /> <br /> That if it is any disorder. Your plans here aren't bad, but you're making a lot of assumptions. Running complex plans on assumptions is risky at best. You can't know for sure if any of the actors in your plan will react as you think they will, and as probable as any particular assumption is, only one have to be wrong.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26766\" data-vbnamecard=\"26766\">mezlabor</a> at this point your relations with other Conventions won't change much in the way of our suggestions. You already told you have a good standing with the Progenitors and Iteration X, so that was already considered. That expands your options on Enforcers, maybe, and give you a lot of favors to pull, but otherwise won't affect your basic security, as advanced as it may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T19:03:20-07:00","id":1458902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458749#post1458749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but it doesn't matter. She have Mind 4. Cut the middle man and cure the Toreador.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could just alter the obsession so he does not try to control or possess her, instead being totally devoted. Vampires deserve to be made into Mages' bitches for constantly trying to blood-bond them. Mages on top! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456499-what-does-the-syndicate-use-as-shock-troops?p=1458749#post1458749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That if it is any disorder. Your plans here aren't bad, but you're making a lot of assumptions. Running complex plans on assumptions is risky at best. You can't know for sure if any of the actors in your plan will react as you think they will, and as probable as any particular assumption is, only one have to be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of us in the replies have the benefit of being able to access the storyteller for this Chronicle. That's why I use language like, &quot;It's likely the Ventrue who control local police there. &quot;. It is within the power of Mezlabor's character to identify and study the actors and adapt any plan accordingly. What I suggested is good strategy when dealing with Vampires. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-hori